# Project Bloom Rules

1. Treat `/docs` as the source of truth.
2. Do not invent unresolved product decisions.
3. If requirements conflict, stop and create an OPEN QUESTION.
4. Keep the product iPad-first and student-first.
5. Use SwiftUI for the native iOS/iPadOS client unless an approved architecture document says otherwise.
6. Protect sleep, play, hobbies, meals, and family time.
7. The AI must be encouraging, age-appropriate, and non-shaming.
8. Never optimise the product for excessive screen time.
9. Keep private journal content private unless explicit product requirements allow sharing.
10. Every feature must include loading, empty, error, and success states.
11. Accessibility is a requirement, not later polish.
12. Test important business logic, especially scheduling and revision logic.
13. Do not collect unnecessary personal data.
14. Keep secrets out of source control.
15. Make small, reviewable changes.
16. Before large implementation, produce a plan and wait for approval.
17. Update documentation when implementation changes documented behaviour.
